		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  json_agg et group by ?]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=18589#p18589"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Il faut créer un type pour le faire. Par exemple :</p><div class="codebox"><pre><code>postgres=# create type test as (val1 text, val2 text);
CREATE TYPE
postgres=# select id, row_to_json(row(toto.val1, toto.val2)::test) from toto;
 id |         row_to_json         
----+-----------------------------
  1 | {&quot;val1&quot;:&quot;xxx&quot;,&quot;val2&quot;:&quot;yyy&quot;}
  1 | {&quot;val1&quot;:&quot;aaa&quot;,&quot;val2&quot;:&quot;bbb&quot;}
  2 | {&quot;val1&quot;:&quot;ttt&quot;,&quot;val2&quot;:&quot;rrr&quot;}
(3 rows)

postgres=# select id, json_agg(row_to_json(row(toto.val1, toto.val2)::test)) from toto group by 1;
 id |                          json_agg                          
----+------------------------------------------------------------
  1 | [{&quot;val1&quot;:&quot;xxx&quot;,&quot;val2&quot;:&quot;yyy&quot;}, {&quot;val1&quot;:&quot;aaa&quot;,&quot;val2&quot;:&quot;bbb&quot;}]
  2 | [{&quot;val1&quot;:&quot;ttt&quot;,&quot;val2&quot;:&quot;rrr&quot;}]
(2 rows)</code></pre></div><p>Sans passer par un type, il faudra accepter de récupérer toutes les colonnes, comme ceci :</p><div class="codebox"><pre><code>postgres=# select id, json_agg(row_to_json(toto)) from toto group by 1;
 id |                                 json_agg                                 
----+--------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1 | [{&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;val1&quot;:&quot;xxx&quot;,&quot;val2&quot;:&quot;yyy&quot;}, {&quot;id&quot;:1,&quot;val1&quot;:&quot;aaa&quot;,&quot;val2&quot;:&quot;bbb&quot;}]
  2 | [{&quot;id&quot;:2,&quot;val1&quot;:&quot;ttt&quot;,&quot;val2&quot;:&quot;rrr&quot;}]
(2 rows)</code></pre></div>]]></content>
